    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0707" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg695"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/8–2745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-27T17:00:00+03:00">August 27, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 27—10:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3073. Supplementing my 3069, August 27. I asked General Deane when he saw
                    Generals Antonov and Slavin<anchor n="43" xml:id="d481-f1"/> Saturday night to
                    point out that the text of General Order No. 1 transmitted with his letter of
                    August 19 included the surrender of the Kurile Islands to the Soviet commander.
                    Antonov appeared confused and said “You are now advising me of this”. Deane
                    reiterated that he had before him the actual text submitted on August 10. Both
                    Antonov and Slavin appeared so embarrassed and concerned that General Deane said
                    “I suppose with all the translation you have had to make in the last few days
                    you missed this”. Neither Antonov nor Slavin took exception to this remark.</p>
                <p>General Deane and I believe therefore that the General Staff slipped up in
                    information given the Foreign Office with regard to the inclusion of this
                    provision.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d481-f1" n="43" xml:id="d481-f1-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. Nikolay Vasilyevich Slavin, Assistant to Gen. Antonov, Chief of the
                    Soviet Army General Staff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
